<title>GERMANY: E.German June adjusted jobless rises 12,000.</title>
<headline>E.German June adjusted jobless rises 12,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Jun 97	 May 97	   Jun 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.298 mln    1.295 mln	1.119 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.333 mln    1.321 mln	1.157 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+12,000	+29,000	  -6,000</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		17.3 pct     17.2 pct	 15.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	47,350	 54,210	   60,646</p>
<p> Vacancies		   59,555	 51,957	   61,392</p>
<p> Change in number in work Apr 97	Mar 96</p>
<p>				-16,000	 + 9,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
